Subject: [PATCH] jasmine-j0154: display off puts the panel to sleep and stops the MDP timing engine; touch pauses

Screen off on jasmine only switched the WLED off: the MDP kept scanning a frame out of DDR at
30 Hz into an awake panel, and touch was polled over I2C every 10 ms. Now, as the stock mdss
driver for the tianma nt36672 video panel: WLED off, DCS 0x28, 20 ms, 0x10 sleep in, 120 ms,
INTF_1 timing engine off. On: timing engine on (before the redraw), 0x11, 120 ms, 0x29, WLED.
Supplies and reset stay, so sleep-in keeps the panel's init registers. DSI commands go through
the DSI0 command DMA (as topaz) from 16 KiB after flip buffer 0 in the splash reservation.
The touch thread (NT36672 = touch and display in one chip) stops polling while the panel
sleeps and checks the chip id again on display on (reset pulse if it does not answer).
sweetfb_pipeoff=0: the old backlight-only display off.
---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_nvt.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_nvt.c
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_nvt.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_nvt.c
@@ -236,6 +236,22 @@ nvt_reset_pulse(void)
 	pin_rst[1] = 2;
 }
 
+/*
+ * j0154: the NT36672 is one chip for touch and display; with the panel in sleep-in
+ * (SweetFramebuffer jasmine display off) touch is off too. The thread stops polling
+ * (no I2C every 10 ms with the screen off) and checks the chip again on display on.
+ */
+static volatile int nvt_display_off;
+void sweet_nvt_display(int on);
+void
+sweet_nvt_display(int on)
+{
+	nvt_display_off = !on;
+	if (on) {
+		thread_wakeup((event_t)&nvt_display_off);
+	}
+}
